WEBVTT

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>The year was 1889.</i>

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.320
<i>Jean, Nadia and King were set adrift on the ocean</i>

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.190
<i>after attacks by mysterious sea monsters.</i>

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:38.200
<i>They were saved by Captain Nemo in the fantastic submarine Nautilus.</i>

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.660
<i>The Nautilus was pursuing another submarine, the real monsters.</i>

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.330
<i>Jean wanted to see the interior of the Nautilus, but this was denied.</i>

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.000
<i>Everything was kept very secret from them.</i>

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.840
<i>The Nautilus finally overtook its prey who launched a counter-attack.</i>

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.510
<i>After a fierce battle, the Nautilus lost sight of the enemy submarine.</i>

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.390
<i>Several days later, the three were released in Jean's aircraft</i>

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.470
<i>now repaired and converted into a seaplane.</i>

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.680
<i>They took off to continue their adventures.</i>

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.400
This is a marvelous engine.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.990
We have a full tank. What more can we ask for?

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.410
I didn't realize flying felt so good.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.210
Why don't we circle the island before landing?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:35.170
But it may be better to land right away before we have trouble again.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.430
Girls just don't understand the romance of flying through the sky.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.280
Easy with the food. Leave some for me.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.700
I don't see how anyone can eat things like this.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.580
I wonder when we can sit down to a real dinner?

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.040
I wonder?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.460
How did we end up like this chasing after the Blue Water?

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.880
I wonder?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:27.390
You wonder? It's all because you two couldn't handle one small girl!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.520
I still wonder.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:36.230
Why am I so unlucky when it comes to men?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:42.160
On top of that, we get cast ashore on an uncivilized island like this.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.580
Dear God, please tell me, have I done anything wrong?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.330
Oh, lots.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:54.420
It's a bad sign if you can't remember things like that.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.630
Hey, this food tastes lousy!

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.340
You always say one thing too many!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.050
I'm sorry.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.310
We still don't have the Blue Water.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.350
Are we going to end our lives on this island?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:20.820
It sure looks that way, but where can the Blue Water be?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:24.360
What's that?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.490
An aircraft?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.370
That aircraft!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.500
It's the Blue Water!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.960
What's wrong?

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.300
I got the feeling that something bad is going to happen.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.180
Nadia, this is where my skill comes in.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.550
Landing is the most difficult part.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.470
Your skill?

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.430
But Jean, isn't this the first time for you?

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:57.100
That's why I said it takes skill.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.480
No more crash landings, please.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.360
Don't worry.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:04.320
What? What's that big hole?

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.570
There's a big pile of slag ahead,

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.080
so it must be an open mine of some kind.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.550
It's smoking.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.130
Yeah.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.510
It's been hit by a shell.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.220
Looks like this island is inhabited.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.890
Yes, they must be bad guys trying to steal the Blue Water.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.980
Sort of like you, right?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.400
Sanson! Hanson!

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.560
Go after that aircraft right away!

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.980
And rescue Nadia?

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.190
You fool! This is a perfect chance to grab the Blue Water.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.490
But the Gratan will be ready in just a little while.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.620
Which is more important: her life or the Gratan?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.370
So it's really not the Blue Water.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.960
You! You talk too much too!

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.250
So, I am right.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.630
Come on! Let's go!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:06.760
Roger!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.270
Darn it!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.420
They were brave kids.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.140
Amen.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.480
King? King?

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.570
Where are you?

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.700
I see. You fell off the aircraft, didn't you?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.160
Aircraft...

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.370
Jean? King?

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.540
Jean, King! Please answer me!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.340
It's burning?

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:52.660
Jean!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.160
Jean...

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.540
Nadia...

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.710
Thank goodness.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.080
Nadia, where's my airplane?

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.460
Over there.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.970
All broken up again?

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.300
Say, where's King?

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.850
I can't find him anywhere.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.180
I see! Let's go look for him right away!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.640
But before that...

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.270
What is it, Jean?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.110
I'd be greatful if you could help me get up.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.070
This is really terrible.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.740
The body is all broken up.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:39.450
What about Nadia?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.700
Not much hope for her, I guess.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.380
Don't move!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:52.050
Don't move or you'll die. Throw your guns down and do as I say.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.670
Can't be helped.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.560
Can they start shooting without warning?

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.440
This island is supposed to be a peaceful place.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.690
I only hope King is safe.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:11.940
What is it?

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.610
There are bodies on the ground.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.790
Sir, hello? Hello?

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.420
He's cold!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.550
Blood...

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.270
Nadia!

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.740
The dog probably belongs to them too.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.890
Jean, the girl is alive!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.640
Someone's coming. Nadia, we'd better hide!

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.440
It's Grandis and her men.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.320
I wonder what they're doing here?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.620
Yeah, those soldiers are all carrying guns.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.620
They must be the ones that killed the man and his wife.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.750
What are they?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.420
A gang of killers!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.920
It's dangerous to stay here.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.960
We'd better move, Nadia.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:54.750
Yes...

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.090
Have they found us?

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.930
Nadia!

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:04.850
King?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.730
You're all right! I was so worried!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.440
You're tickling me!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.870
I wonder if she knows what happened to her parents?

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.840
I think she's waking up.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.260
Really?

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.520
Mama?

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.940
No, my name is Nadia.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.770
And this is Jean.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:55.560
What's your name?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:56.900
Marie!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:02.610
Don't be afraid, Marie! This is King, a baby lion.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.950
A lion?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.740
He wants to become friends with you.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.790
You're tickling me!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.630
Where's my Mama?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.590
She's not here right now.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.840
Then where's Papa?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.840
Papa's not here either.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.220
I want to go to Mama and Papa.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:26.970
You can't right now.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:32.100
Why not? Papa said we're going to hide in the old village.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:32.980
Village?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:37.820
Yes, it's not far from here. Marie remembers clearly!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.650
Of course you do, Marie. You're a good girl.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.610
Mama said so.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:50.620
What's this?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.830
Let's go to that village.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.330
Hey...

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.220
What's that? An aircraft, you said?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.850
Yes, Sir. We shot down an unidentified aircraft

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.020
that was circling over the island in the M32 district.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:17.730
It went up in smoke. We are searching for survivors.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:21.730
I see. Use all means to locate the survivors.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.450
Yes, Sir! We also captured an odd trio near the scene of the crash.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.410
What shall we do with them?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.700
Bring them here. I want to interrogate them.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.160
Yes, Sir!

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.540
I can't think of anyone having an aircraft other than us.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:39.380
Maybe they're from the Nautilus.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.430
It's really true!

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:53.270
Mama's cooking is the best in the world.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.980
I see. Isn't that nice?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:14:00.860
Isn't it? When you come to our house, she'll make a wonderful dinner for you.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:07.200
I wonder why Papa and Mama don't come?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.370
They were in such a hurry.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.750
Say, Marie, what did your papa do?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.000
He was an engineer at the power plant.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.080
Power plant?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:24.210
Don't you know? It's where they burn coal to make lots of electricity.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:29.300
A thermo-electric power plant? Why is there something like that here?

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.510
Say, Marie, you said they were in a hurry.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.600
Why was that?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:41.440
I don't know. Marie was sleeping when Mama woke me up.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.610
I thought it was time to go to the toilet.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:45.980
And then?

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:50.740
Papa and Mama seemed awfully worried. And then...

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.290
We ran deeper and deeper into the woods.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.540
And then...

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:02.080
There were lots of scary people behind us, chasing us.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.630
And then there was a terrible noise.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.800
Then...

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.470
Papa and Mama went to sleep.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.310
Mookie went to sleep too.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:19.270
I don't remember anything after that.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:24.060
But Mama's hand got colder and colder. That I remember.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:32.490
You don't have to say any more.
I'm sorry. That's enough.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.590
They've found us!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.930
I'm sorry.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.520
I wonder how they found us?

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:07.610
It must be that. The candle over there.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.610
We know you're in there!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:15.370
Come out with your hands up.
I'm going to count to five.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.700
One!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.830
Darn them!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.330
Two...

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.710
Three...

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:25.880
Right!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:26.790
What is it?

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:27.960
Four...

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:30.300
Fi...

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:34.090
Wait! We're coming out! Don't shoot!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.010
Okay, that's a good boy.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.720
When they come out, let them have it.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.220
Yes, Sir!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.240
Damn, there they go!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.400
Don't let them get away!

00:16:59.160 --> 00:16:59.830
Get under cover!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.790
Right!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.290
There he goes!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.420
He jumped into the river by himself. Go after him!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.760
Yes, Sir!

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.390
Do you see him?

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.010
No, Sir!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.350
All right! Go on that side!

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.760
Yes, Sir!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.440
How many were there?

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:28.860
Sir, three kids and one cat.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.730
They may not be from this island.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.740
On the other hand, I can't imagine a kid flying an aircraft.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.070
We better report to the commander. Let's head back to base.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:39.740
Yes, Sir!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.670
What shall we do now?

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:52.340
We can't build a fire, they'll see it.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.880
At night, we're supposed to go to the cave.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.510
A cave?

00:17:56.510 --> 00:18:00.640
Don't you know? It's that big one on the other side of the cape.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:04.430
We're supposed to go there, and meet Papa's friends.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.640
Papa's friends?

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:07.690
That's right.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:11.060
There must've been others trying to escape too.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:15.190
Let's go to the cave. We may be able to meet them.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.360
Will Papa and Mama be there too?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.450
Yes, we may be able to meet them there.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:23.830
Let's go.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.250
What? You found the intruders?

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:33.420
Yes, Sir! We found three kids and one cat that probably came on the aircraft.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.170
We are searching for them now.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.630
You let them escape?

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.590
I'm sorry, Sir.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:39.680
That's okay.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:45.970
Change of orders! Take the girl alive. You can kill all the rest.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:46.680
Yes, Sir!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.190
It seems their number increased by one,

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.900
but I guess you haven't been lying to us.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.490
That's what I've been trying to tell you!

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:01.280
We were only after the Blue Water, and landed on this island.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.780
Where did you learn about the Blue Water?

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.290
I saw it on a poster some time back.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.170
It must be that poster we gave out.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:13.170
I guess it served some purpose.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:18.010
Haven't we told you enough? Please let us go!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:19.760
Not yet!

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.930
You are our special guests.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:24.640
You're going to work here for the rest of your lives.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.430
You've got to be kidding!
That's not part of our agreement!

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:28.310
Take them away!

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:28.930
Yes, Sir!

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:36.940
We can't allow anyone to tell the outside world this island's secret.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.580
Water and food...

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.250
They really intended to escape from here.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:51.040
But there's no one.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.880
I guess they haven't arrived yet, or

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.090
they can't come anymore.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.590
Jean, look. There are blankets here.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.140
Cover Marie with one.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.900
Well, let's get some sleep too.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.650
A lot of things happened today.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.620
Jean, are you awake?

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.380
Yeah, I can't sleep.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:40.090
I see.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.610
Jean, what's wrong?

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.610
I'm going outside for a minute.

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.190
Where to?

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:06.820
There's something I must do before Marie wakes up in the morning.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.830
I'll be right back.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.120
Wait, I'm coming with you.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.580
No, you must stay here.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:16.630
Jean...

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.540
You can't do it all by yourself.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.220
All right, let's go.

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.450
Papa... Mama...

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:18.400
Marie...

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:19.690
Listen carefully.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:20.440
What is it?

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:23.400
Well...

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.860
Your Papa and Mama have passed away.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.570
Passed away?

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:34.620
Yes, they have gone far away into the sky to Heaven.

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.040
Mookie too?

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:38.370
Yes, Mookie has gone with them.

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:39.790
Then Marie wants to go there too!

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:43.300
No, you can't. You must stay here with us.

00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:46.800
No, I want to be with Papa and Mama!

00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:49.130
Marie, please listen to me.

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:51.600
No! No! Marie wants to go too!

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:52.600
You can't!

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:53.430
Jean!

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:56.350
It's not a place you can go.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:58.310
You mustn't go!

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:06.070
You can't see them anymore, Marie. Can't you see?

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:09.610
Jean...

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.580
I can't see them anymore?

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.670
No, I don't believe you. No!

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:33.050
Marie wants to go too!
